WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.700
There was a mathematician named Klein

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.440
who thought Möbius bands are divine. Said

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.920
he, if you glue the edges of two you get

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.420
the weird bottle like mine.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.599
You're probably familiar with a Möbius

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:21.899
band. It's the special shape where, if you

00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:24.179
run your finger on the surface you start

00:00:24.179 --> 00:00:26.160
here on the outside you're running it

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.340
along the surface, and magically you're

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.410
ending up on the other side. So we

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.360
have been able to go from one side of

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.589
the surface to the other without

00:00:34.589 --> 00:00:36.390
actually stepping over the edge; we just

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.210
did it by going once around the loop. So

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.430
if we were to start spreading paint

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.079
from here and we just paint and paint

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:44.909
and paint that surface, we'll actually

00:00:44.909 --> 00:00:48.030
end up painting everything. And so this

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.780
is called a single sided surface, or

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.559
mathematicians also call it and

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:57.360
non-orientable surface. Just one face, one

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.159
paint colour needed to paint everything.

00:01:01.159 --> 00:01:04.670
Now, this particular surface has an edge.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.619
So here is an edge, let's see. If we go

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:10.020
along this particular edge, I'm running

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.060
around here I'm going through my hand,

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.250
I'm on the bottom side now, and I'm going

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.320
through the bottom of the edge and

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.049
suddenly I come back up again. 
So it's only

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:22.979
a single edge but the edge actually goes

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:26.280
twice around that loop. So we have a

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.420
single sided surface, with a single edge.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.890
Now the single sided surface is pretty

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.140
intriguing; we got from one side of the

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.010
surface to the other without having to

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.440
drill through the surface, or without

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.260
having to step across the edge. Is it

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.140
possible to make a single sided surface

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.110
that has no edges - that's kind of closed?

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:50.580
Just like a sphere has no edges, right,

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.500
it's a closed surface. But in a sphere to

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.060
get from the inside to the outside

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.619
you clearly have to drill through the

00:01:55.619 --> 00:01:57.960
surface. So can we make a single sided

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.090
surface that has no edges? That you could

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.130
step over? And where it seems impossible

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:05.090
to get from one side to the other. You

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:09.179
can - it's called a Klein bottle. 
This is a

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:13.260
Klein bottle. Now, how this is- what we

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.150
said before apply, is this really single

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.610
sided? Assume that you're an ant and now

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.730
the ant is walking on the outside of the

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.650
bulb and getting to the outside of the

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.049
handle, walking around the outside of the

00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:27.359
handle, walking on the outside of the

00:02:27.359 --> 00:02:29.459
handle and penetrating through the wall

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:30.900
but staying on the outside of the

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.540
handle on this inner part. And you now, if

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.010
you imagine that you're on the outside

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.079
of this inner handle you're now inside

00:02:37.079 --> 00:02:39.209
this bulb. So as you walk around the

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:40.860
bottom you're still on the inside, and you

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.720
can walk all around the inside of this

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.659
bulb. You can then continue on the inside

00:02:45.659 --> 00:02:47.970
of the bulb walking into the inside of

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.680
the handle, now you're walking on the

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.450
inside of the tunnel all the way around

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.849
the loop. You're staying on the inside of

00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:57.120
the handle and you're coming out. And 
you're

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.250
back on the outside again. So it is

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.409
indeed possible to get from one side of

00:03:01.409 --> 00:03:02.910
the glass surface to the other.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.859
(Brady: But didn't you pass- 
like you didn't drill a)

00:03:04.859 --> 00:03:06.150
(hole but wouldn't you have needed to)

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.950
(drill a-)
- Ahh you caught me,

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.010
okay, unfortunately there are no Klein

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.049
bottles that have no so-called self

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:15.540
intersections. The Klein bottle really is

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.099
a mathematical construct that you could

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:18.900
do in four dimensional space without any

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.689
intersections. Any kind of Klein bottle

00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:23.370
that you want to do in three-dimensional

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.170
space does indeed have some kind of

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.209
penetration. Now the rule for

00:03:27.209 --> 00:03:30.030
mathematicians is: where two surfaces

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:33.329
like that the, branches go through one

00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:37.230
another, they're completely unaware and

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.000
oblivious that they're branching. You're

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.500
basically allowed to stay on your

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.389
surface; you cannot step from one to the

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:44.340
other. But of course implicitly

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.349
as you go on this surface through the

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:47.970
other one you basically have gone from

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.220
one side to the other and that's why the

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.179
Klein bottle works in three 
dimensional space.

00:03:52.179 --> 00:03:53.970
(Brady: So in the rules of mathematics the)

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.000
(ant doesn't need a drill to get
through here?)

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.919
It doesn't even know that there is this

00:03:58.919 --> 00:04:00.239
other surface coming through. It just

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:02.669
walks basically on that surface and it

00:04:02.669 --> 00:04:05.069
sees no no other surface except the one

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:07.379
that it's walking on. And so that's how

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.060
it gets magically from one side to the

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.579
other. So that is kind of the simplest

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:14.819
form of a Klein bottle, it is made by

00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:18.090
Cliff Stoll of ACME Klein bottles in

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.729
Berkeley. And he has an amazing amount of

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:22.440
different Klein bottles you can get

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.909
from him, you know, just go to his website

00:04:23.909 --> 00:04:28.169
ACME Klein bottles. And for instance, you

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:30.419
know what the stein is? The kind of thing

00:04:30.419 --> 00:04:31.889
they have in your Hofbräu house at the

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:33.580
Oktoberfest?
- (Brady: Oh I love the Hofbräu house!)

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.730
There is your stein except

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:36.780
it's a small stein. But it's a special

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.300
stein, it's a Klein stein. If you look

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.760
closely down here you can see it seems

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.950
to have a double wall, and indeed it does

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.879
have a double wall.

00:04:44.879 --> 00:04:47.939
So now if you pour a liquid up on top

00:04:47.939 --> 00:04:50.580
inside, and then you find that there's a

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.470
hole here that goes from the inner

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.379
volume into the handle. And so by the

00:04:55.379 --> 00:04:57.840
time the liquid reaches that little hole

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.810
and runs down the handle it will pour

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.300
into the interstitial space between the

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.520
inner and the outer cylinder, and it fills

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.639
the outer space. So you realise the

00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:12.810
potential; you basically fill in coffee

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.840
into the outside and you fill in brandy

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.210
on the inside and you're sitting happily

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.620
in your office, and when your boss comes

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.690
by you swear that you're drinking

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.849
coffee but you're enjoying yourself very

00:05:23.849 --> 00:05:25.770
much with what's on the inner part of it.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:28.830
So this is a Klein stein. Topologically

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.659
it is exactly like this Klein bottle

00:05:30.659 --> 00:05:32.039
just has a different shape, you know

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:33.659
there's this extra bulb kind of stuffed

00:05:33.659 --> 00:05:36.779
in, but other than that it's exactly the

00:05:36.779 --> 00:05:38.460
same deal. You know you can walk

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.560
basically on one surface and then go

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:45.389
around the handle, make this unofficial

00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:47.759
kind of transition through the glass

00:05:47.759 --> 00:05:49.469
surface and get essentially from one

00:05:49.469 --> 00:05:50.250
side to the other.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:54.210
So still a Klein bottle, it's still a

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:59.190
single sided surface that has no edges

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.949
per se. So here is my Klein stein and we

00:06:01.949 --> 00:06:03.300
want to see what happens when we pour a

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.520
liquid into it, have a little bit of

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.229
coffee. And we start to fill in and at

00:06:10.229 --> 00:06:12.240
the beginning everything is normal and

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:16.469
nothing special happens. So now, so far

00:06:16.469 --> 00:06:18.569
everything is just as it would be in an

00:06:18.569 --> 00:06:20.759
ordinary stein. But now as we pour in

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:24.180
more liquid see what happens when you

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:28.229
get to the handle - oh no it starts to run

00:06:28.229 --> 00:06:32.430
down the handle here, okay. So now we have

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.849
a trapped air volume up here, right? And

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:37.849
it's kind of hard to now fill it without

00:06:37.849 --> 00:06:40.650
kind of you know shaking a little bit

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:42.419
and let's try and get the air bubbles

00:06:42.419 --> 00:06:44.789
out. So that's kind of a problem, so maybe

00:06:44.789 --> 00:06:46.650
we already filled too much so what we

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:49.289
should do is pour out a little bit more.

00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:55.610
And now that we have more flexibility

00:06:55.610 --> 00:07:02.000
we can get- so it's a little bit hard to

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.919
set up your your coffee cup on the

00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:05.570
outside with then the brandy on the

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.490
inside as you as you can see but so

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:13.190
gradually we're getting a higher filling

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:16.160
level here on the outside. A Klein

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.250
bottle is made from two Möbius bands.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.600
Remember, a Möbius band is a single sided

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.720
surface but it has that one edge. Now, if

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.270
you take two Möbius bands, a red one and

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:27.830
a green one, and they both have just

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.470
one edge. And now you're starting to fuse

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.720
those edges together and you kind of

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.630
zipper them along those edges right? What

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:38.060
d'you get? Well all the edges have

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.770
disappeared, it's like taking two disks

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.300
right and the two disks have two edges and

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.250
you glue the two disks together, they

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.280
form a sphere. But if you do that here,

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:49.160
yes we get rid of all the edges, but it's

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.870
still single sided because each piece

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.460
itself was single side in the first place.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:55.040
So we get a single sided surface that

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.050
has no edges; actually we get a Klein

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.240
bottle. Here is something that also Cliff

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.040
Stoll made: well it looks sort of like a

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.020
Klein bottle. So here is the bulge,

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.780
right, and here is that handle, And here

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.300
is that kind of transition where the

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:12.140
handle essentially goes through that

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.440
surface and goes inside that bulb. Now

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.410
the beauty of this object is that

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.350
somewhere here is a zipper. Now if I can

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.390
find the beginning of the zipper - there

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.539
it is - so now we can open that zipper,

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:28.940
that's like cutting the Klein bottle

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:34.270
into two parts. So I'm zipping open.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.660
You have to go twice around the loop

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.630
remember, that these loops here on the

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:40.370
Möbius band they go twice around. So

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.930
basically I have to zip twice around

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.450
here. See, now I'm coming on my second

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:49.550
pass here; and then it falls apart. Oh my

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:50.630
God, what have I got here?

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.080
I have this band right? And the band

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.839
somehow looks twisted. And yes of course

00:08:56.839 --> 00:08:58.520
it varies in width, it starts out narrow

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.350
and it gets through the white part which

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.660
then forms the bulb; but there's clearly

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.270
a twist of 180 degree right about here,

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.400
so this is a Möbius band.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.970
And the other half is essentially its

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:16.560
mirror image. So, here again is a Möbius

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.360
band; and we have seen the two together

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.100
essentially form the Klein bottle. So

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:26.970
that shows how a Klein bottle is formed

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:30.230
from two Möbius Bands. Here again is an

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:33.090
ordinary-looking kind of Klein bottle,

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.970
okay, I made the bulb a little narrower

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.190
and I put more emphasis basically on the

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:40.110
handle here. And you can see that's the

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:42.330
place where the handle goes back into

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.430
the bulb. I think that's kind of the way

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:47.580
these two things look. Now if you

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.600
look at the handle you can see that the

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.610
the lines here in the handle are

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.640
essentially twisted. So in glass you

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.350
cannot see that where it's twisted or

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.820
not but if you put this structure on

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.980
there you can actually give it a twist;

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.780
I put the twist of a full turn of

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.630
360 degrees. And then I cut it apart

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.840
along a line, not like the other Klein

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:11.910
bottle which I had split simply smack

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:14.850
down the symmetry plane, but I essentially

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:17.550
cut it down along one of those twisted

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.620
spiral things and look what happens; I

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:26.000
basically get two of those thingys

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.580
interlocking now and each one

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.130
individually is essentially a Möbius

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.230
ban. You can see it's a band that

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.330
starts here, it warps around and then it

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:39.630
makes a 180 degree flip up here. So

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.340
here again is another way of

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:45.810
essentially turning a Klein bottle into

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.820
two Möbius bands, but because of the

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:50.040
twists that I put into the handle, now

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.260
the two Möbius bands are actually

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:55.860
intertwined. So most people who have

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.240
heard about Klein bottles probably have

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.680
seen a picture of that, that's the most

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:01.230
familiar one. But actually mathematicians

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:02.790
tell you there's more than just one

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:07.260
Klein bottle and this is also a Klein

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.300
bottle. At first glance it looks kind of

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.420
weird and jumbled, you know 
what's going on?

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.910
Well, what's going on is that we make

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:17.670
ourselves a tube, like we have here, but

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:19.710
the tube now is not having a circular

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:21.100
cross-section

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.680
but we make ourselves a tube that has a

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.500
figure-eight cross-section like that. And

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.020
you can see if we had to do that and you

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:32.740
colour it then if you paint red on the

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:35.380
one half of this figure eight the red

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.660
would go through that junction and be on

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.670
the inside of the other loop; and then

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.290
green would be on the outside here and

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:43.360
green would be on the other side. So if

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.360
we take this two colour tube and we flip

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.040
it around in a big circle and showing it

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.840
back to itself, red goes to red green

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:51.820
goes to green, it still would be a

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:55.030
torus; just an ordinary torus. But if you

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:57.130
take this figure eight and we rotate it

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:59.740
180 degrees and then join it back to

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.500
itself, well the red lobe joins with the

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.150
green lobe, the green lobe joins with the

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.160
red lobe. And we have the same situation

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.830
we had before that if you start painting

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.380
and just paint and paint, before you know

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:12.880
it you have painted everything. So we're

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.040
back to a single sided surface; that's

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.110
exactly what we have here. So if you

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.720
focus in on that part you can see

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:20.320
essentially this figure eight

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:21.820
cross-section which I mentioned before.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:24.400
And I very carefully made sure that

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:26.200
right here at the intersection line, if

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.050
you look at the lines that come from one

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:31.120
side they're going through that

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.650
cross-section without touching the other

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:35.230
ones. Again, that confirms that

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.360
mathematical notion that there where

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.330
surfaces cross you cannot step from one

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:42.040
to the other, they're kind of oblivious

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:44.770
of one from the other okay? So this is

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.810
our figure right cross section. Now we're

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:47.860
swinging this figure eight cross

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.720
section around the loop, and while doing

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:52.930
so we must make sure we have an odd

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.480
number of flips. We could get, you know, a

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:59.170
single flip from here going once around,

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.120
a single 180 degree flip but in

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.400
this case I actually have elected to do

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.650
three flips. So here it is in that

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.020
configuration, it flips and here again

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:10.480
it's facing up to you it flips once more

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.760
to here, and then once more to here; so

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.480
three times 180 degree flip - also make

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.810
sure that one of those lobes when you

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:21.520
come around you're on the other lobe. And

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:23.110
that makes it into a single sided

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:25.870
surface and that again is a Klein

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.460
bottle; there are no edges, it's single

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:29.920
sided. It happens to same kind of

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:32.290
connectivity as this particular
Klein bottle.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.240
- (Brady: It seems very different from
that one.)

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:37.209
It is quite different. 
And particularly the

00:13:37.209 --> 00:13:40.120
mathematicians in this case when you ask

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:42.520
them why are they different, they say

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.230
because there's no way that you can

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.620
smoothly transform this object into that

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.770
object. They have a fancy name, they call

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:54.459
something a regular homotopy if it is

00:13:54.459 --> 00:13:57.160
possible, to by only smoothly deforming

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.560
thing, never ever have any sharp creases,

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.630
never ever doing this kind of thing

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.890
where you have a loop and then you just

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:05.260
kind of get rid of that loop - that's not

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:06.940
allowed. As long as you smoothly deform

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.160
things, no matter how much you stretch

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.070
and compress that's a regular homotopy.

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:15.820
And two things are sort of equal or in the

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:17.589
same regular homotopy class if you

00:14:17.589 --> 00:14:19.959
can transform them. You cannot transform

00:14:19.959 --> 00:14:22.000
that into this, that's why these Klein

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.360
bottles are different. Now if you look at

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.700
this, it has clearly a handedness to it.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.399
It sort of rotates- in this
case I think if

00:14:30.399 --> 00:14:32.560
you go forward it rotates

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:34.899
counterclockwise as you as you kind of

00:14:34.899 --> 00:14:37.209
smoothly go forward, you can see that

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:41.110
cross-section rotating sort of 
counter clockwise, okay?

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.959
The mirror image of that is in a

00:14:43.959 --> 00:14:47.140
different regular homotopy class. You

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:49.720
cannot transform that into its mirror
image.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.870
The reason is basically you cannot

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.640
take a Möbius band and smoothly

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:57.010
transform it into its mirror image, it

00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:58.810
has a handedness built-in. And

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.779
remember, Klein bottles are built from two

00:15:01.779 --> 00:15:05.860
Möbius bands. Turns out the regular Klein

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:08.050
bottle here is built from one

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.690
right-handed, one left-handed Möbius band;

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:12.940
we've seen that before, we had those two

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.529
Möbius bands and when they fell apart

00:15:14.529 --> 00:15:16.120
they were mirror images, a right one and

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:20.860
a left one. So here, if you have

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.440
something that is a figure eight that

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.950
twists right handed, you cut it apart in

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:29.290
the middle it essentially composes into

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:32.079
two right-handed Möbius bands. The other

00:15:32.079 --> 00:15:35.290
one falls into two left-handed Möbius

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:37.750
bands, okay? So we already have three

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.750
different regular homotopies for Klein

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.310
bottles. Three different Klein bottles.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:45.010
Well, that was known in a paper going

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.980
back to about 30 years by Hass

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:50.530
and Hughes; and they make one more

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:52.570
observation. They say if you essentially

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.580
put a structure like this coordinate

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.260
grid we have or some colour on the

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:59.020
surface, then there are four different

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:02.890
Klein bottles. And that really intrigued

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:05.320
me. So I I set out, you know, several

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:07.090
months of my life to find- I want to

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.500
find that fourth Klein bottle. Now that

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.840
mathematical paper was above my horizon,

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:12.940
I couldn't follow all the logics that

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.560
had to do is group theory and symmetry and

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:16.690
observation and 
the like - I wanted to make

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:18.850
a really nice picture, figure out what's

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:22.420
going on here. And in that process I came

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.610
up with other interesting Klein bottles.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:28.840
So here, what is this? Well it's again a

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:33.250
figure 8 loop, now it forms a trefoil

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:35.290
knot as we've seen before. Actually it is

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:36.520
really no different from that one.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:39.070
Because remember topologists allow you

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:41.470
to smoothly pass surfaces through one

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:44.500
another; in particular a knot makes no

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.840
sense to a topologist because you have

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.900
two strands and, you know, they pass right

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.020
through one another. So you could open

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.790
this trefoil knot into just a simple

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.070
loop and it would then be simply a

00:16:57.070 --> 00:17:00.220
triply twisted figure-eight loop just
like this one.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:03.610
So this - nothing new, it just belongs to

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:05.970
that one.

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:08.320
Searching further for that fourth Klein

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.700
bottle I came up with this wonderful

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:12.250
contraption. I thought this was really

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:16.870
cool because it's sort of like this

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:21.310
thing, only there's of two of them. I call

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.410
this the inverted sock Klein bottle

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.060
because at the end the mouth looks like

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.280
the part of an inverted sock. And this is

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.980
like the inverted double sock, right? 
And I

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.020
thought surely that this is different

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.810
and this must be, you know, the new Klein

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.360
bottle. Well to make a long story short

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:40.360
it isn't. The main reason actually turned

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:44.290
out that this is not its own mirror

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:48.520
image. If I make a mirror image then

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:52.840
it is clearly different, and if you

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.910
analyse this and you 
cut it apart into Möbius

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:57.370
strips you find out it's falling apart

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.820
into two identical Möbius strips,

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:01.680
okay? And so again we have the same

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:02.800
situation; we get essentially a

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.730
right hand left-handed version. So the

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:08.220
logic says if this were something new I

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:10.800
get not just one new thing I get two new

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:13.020
things; a right hand left handed version.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:14.850
But that paper clearly proves they're

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:17.130
only four Klein bottles not five, so this

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.260
must be something known. And since it

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.720
fell apart into two identical Möbius

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.810
bands it really is in disguise that same

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:29.240
thing- object again. So that was not it.

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:32.850
Then I came across this one. This is

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:35.010
indeed another special Klein bottle,

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:38.910
it's due to Lawson who proved that this

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:41.940
is the minimum energy Klein bottle. In

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:45.930
some sense nature would prefer that, it's

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:49.590
like a soap film. Soap films try to take

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:51.750
on the shape that minimises the surface

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.520
area, minimises the built in energy

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:56.250
that's in in the surface. And so if

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:58.920
similarly we were to look at this

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:02.250
surface and there is bending energy

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.990
required to bend it and the more you

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:05.760
bend it the more energy you require;

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:08.340
typically the bending energy of a thin

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:10.730
sheet of metal goes with the square of

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:13.950
curvature. And so if you integrate square

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.040
of curvature over this surface and

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:18.120
compared this to any other Klein bottle

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:20.190
then this one has the lowest possible

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:22.830
energy. I thought that is pretty cool,

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:25.410
maybe that is number four - but again you

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:28.290
can obviously tell by looking at it that

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:30.720
this thing seems to have some chirality

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:33.630
again, so it's not its own mirror image.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:36.150
So again, if this were new there would be

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.160
two of them; you analyse how it breaks

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:40.500
apart in Möbius bands and you find it

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:41.970
breaks apart into identical Möbius

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:44.700
bands so again we're back on that same

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:49.230
heap. Okay, nothing new yet, okay? Phew.

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:52.650
Ah! Now here's an interesting shape. It

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.510
looks like a special Klein bottle, it has

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:56.850
two inverted sock mouths, okay?

00:19:58.291 --> 00:20:00.390
(Brady: That looks like a roller coaster 
or something)

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.550
(that should be at Disneyland)
- Ah it looks fantastic,

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.920
right? Now it turns out it's not even a

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:07.500
Klein bottle. Because here is what

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:09.300
happens, if you start here on the outside

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:12.060
and you go around and you get to the

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.590
inside at this mouth,

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.240
and you go around the inside of the

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.039
handle, inside of the handle, inside of

00:20:17.039 --> 00:20:19.200
the handle and you're coming out here

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:21.840
and you're back where you were. 
This actually

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.580
is two-sided, you could clearly- you know

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:26.309
paint it with one colour on one side and

00:20:26.309 --> 00:20:28.049
this the other - so it's just a torus.

00:20:28.049 --> 00:20:29.850
It's a weird torus, you know that kind

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:31.320
of self intersects and does weird things;

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:34.409
it's not a Klein bottle. So, you have to

00:20:34.409 --> 00:20:35.760
be very careful when you look at these

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.220
things to make sure whether you have a

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:40.380
Klein bottle or whether it's actually a

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:43.740
two sided surface. Sometimes that's not

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:45.899
a recipe that works quite simply, but

00:20:45.899 --> 00:20:49.409
if you have an even number of these kind

00:20:49.409 --> 00:20:51.510
of surface inversion mouths then it's

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.539
just a torus. If you have an odd number

00:20:53.539 --> 00:20:57.330
then it's very likely a Klein bottle. So,

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:00.380
what is this? Is this a Klein bottle?

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:03.690
(Brady: That's a monster.) 
- It's a Klein knot-tle I call it. A

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:06.059
knotted Klein bottle. So I can see we

00:21:06.059 --> 00:21:07.890
have three times the kind of mouth that

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:09.299
we find on the ordinary Klein bottle,

00:21:09.299 --> 00:21:13.830
and it's just kind of hooked together in

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:16.710
such a way that it forms also a trefoil

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:19.289
knot. And so a knotted Klein bottle I

00:21:19.289 --> 00:21:23.340
call a Klein knottle. And it's a perfectly

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:27.400
good Klein bottle. 
- (Brady: Is it the magic one?)

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:31.799
No. It turns out this now brings
us back to

00:21:31.799 --> 00:21:34.440
the ordinary Klein bottle. So it belongs

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.960
essentially to that shape. As a matter of

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:40.620
fact it's very hard to show that number

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:42.480
four because it really relies on the

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:45.120
fact that you need some colouring and you

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:47.190
need to distinguish the longitudinal

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:49.710
edges from the the cross side edges. In

00:21:49.710 --> 00:21:53.750
the end it turned out to be rather

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:57.390
almost disappointingly simple. If you

00:21:57.390 --> 00:22:01.169
take this Klein bottle right? We know we

00:22:01.169 --> 00:22:02.789
could split it in the symmetry plane and

00:22:02.789 --> 00:22:07.020
make two Möbius bands. One half might be

00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:09.120
green the other one would be red, one is

00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:11.640
right oriented or right twisting the

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:13.740
other one is left twisted. All you have

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:16.559
to do is switch colours, okay. Now if you

00:22:16.559 --> 00:22:18.299
switch colours on the two Möbius bands

00:22:18.299 --> 00:22:20.309
you get a Klein bottle that basically

00:22:20.309 --> 00:22:21.780
seems to have the colour reversed. And

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:24.720
there's no way to deform it back into

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:25.770
the other one because they're

00:22:25.770 --> 00:22:26.620
right-handed;

00:22:26.620 --> 00:22:28.480
red band cannot be turned into

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:30.040
right-handed green band - but you

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:31.720
essentially need colours to find that

00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:33.670
fourth Klein bottle. So finally that was

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:35.740
the answer. And it's all in the paper, I

00:22:35.740 --> 00:22:37.630
didn't invent it I just made it

00:22:37.630 --> 00:22:39.160
essentially visible to people; and so

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:40.990
that was my contribution there. I

00:22:40.990 --> 00:22:43.270
actually had it peer-reviewed by those

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:44.770
mathematicians who wrote the original

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:48.880
paper and they loved it. They felt, yeah
I did

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:50.440
fair description of what they did and

00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:53.470
absolutely it was needed to make a more

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:57.220
visible model to have a broader segment

00:22:57.220 --> 00:22:58.929
of the pop- population actually

00:22:58.929 --> 00:23:00.820
understand this, right? And so I may have

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:02.860
taken, you know, from 1 in 10,000 
to 1 in

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:04.270
100 or whatever but that-

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:06.970
that's still an improvement.

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:09.070
[Preview] ...kind of cutting through
and I'm

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:11.170
rotating my knife

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:14.020
all the way around, and then doing it on

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:17.080
the other side; the doughnut 
will still fall

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:22.800
apart into two individual pieces.

